{
    "notes": [
        "Which component modules load together, and so which can stay unloaded until a page needs them (upstream abcaa16d's file, written for this tree's module list).",
        "Every module of js/component-scripts.json that no group here lists belongs to the implicit group \"core\", which every page loads.",
        "The server serves any set of groups as one script (GET /JellyfinEnhanced/bundle.js?g=core,tags; Features/Platform/Services/ClientScriptBundle.cs) and the loader",
        "decides which groups a page needs (FEATURE_GROUPS) and which stage-6 initializer belongs to which group (FEATURE_INITIALIZERS), in client/src/bootstrap/loader/.",
        "Rules: a module is in one group; inside a group modules run in manifest order; \"after\" names groups (listed earlier in this file) whose modules",
        "must have run first, because this group reads their exports while loading or cannot work without them. The order of this file is the order groups",
        "run in when several load together. A new module that is not listed here loads on every page: list it in a group unless every page needs it.",
        "A module of client/shared-modules.json is published by its provider: every script that reads it must be in the provider's group, a group it is after, or core, after the provider (the client build checks this).",
        "Upstream modules this tree folds into another output are not listed: osd-playback and subtitle-sync are in the player group's playback.js and auto-skip.js,",
        "the discovery modules in the seerr group's discovery-filter-utils.js, and maintainerr-item-menu (upstream group removal-menu) and the leaving-soon page and tab",
        "(upstream group leavingsoon-page) in tags/tag-item-menu.js, whose group (tags) therefore loads wherever upstream loads any of those three groups.",
        "tests/frontend/bootstrap/bootstrap-groups.test.mjs checks the split (each group loads with only what it is after); bootstrap-bundle-budget.test.mjs checks the sizes against scripts/bundle-budgets.json."
    ],
